    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as our offensive pillars. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the roster with a 73.99 score, benefiting from a prime #2 hole projection and a favorable matchup against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. Despite minor headwinds from the opponent's catcher and hold-base efficiency, his base projections remain elite. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** provides a robust 66.91 score against Mike Burrows, as the park factors and order placement solidify his role as our primary run-producer. **Nolan Schanuel** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also warrant strong consideration; **Nolan Schanuel** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Trey Gibson (5.27 xERA), while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** maintains an impressive 61.14 rating thanks to a notable BvP history and a dynamic platoon advantage that compensates for his lower batting order position.\n\nWe are monitoring weather volatility for both **Brayan Rocchio** and **Sam Antonacci**, as the 32% rain risk in their respective matchups creates a non-trivial performance ceiling risk. While **Sam Antonacci** remains a solid start with a 60.75 score due to his leadoff duties and favorable xwOBA, any further reports of inclement weather could necessitate a shift. On the bench, **Jacob Wilson** was the most difficult exclusion, posting a 57.24 score that flirted with our starting criteria. Ultimately, the optimizer favored the platoon-adjusted upside and park factors of **Curtis Mead** and **Wade Meckler** over **Jacob Wilson**, though he remains our top insurance piece should any late lineup scratches occur. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages**, as both face high-skill pitchers in Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez and Joe Ryan, respectively, which slightly dampens their expected efficiency compared to our top-tier targets.",
